      "text": "To determine the measure of angle \\( P \\) in the given polygon, we need to understand the properties of the angles and the relationships between them. The angles given in the problem are:\n\n- \\( \\angle A = 128^\\circ \\)\n- \\( \\angle B = 92^\\circ \\)\n- \\( \\angle C = 113^\\circ \\)\n- \\( \\angle D = 111^\\circ \\)\n\nWe know that the sum of the interior angles of a pentagon (which is the shape described) is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of interior angles} = (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( n \\) is the number of sides of the polygon. For a pentagon (\\( n = 5 \\)):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of interior angles} = (5-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 3 \\times 180^\\circ = 540^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNext, we sum the given angles:\n\n\\[\n128^\\circ + 92^\\circ + 113^\\circ + 111^\\circ = 444^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTo find the measure of angle \\( P \\), we subtract the sum of the known angles from the total sum of the interior angles:\n\n\\[\nP = 540^\\circ - 444^\\circ = 96^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of angle \\( P \\) is \\(\\boxed{96^\\circ}\\).",
